## Self-Hosted Fonts

The documentation site serves the following font files from
`docs/assets/fonts/`. Each is a subset of an upstream release file, made by
`scripts/regenerate_fonts.py`, which pins the release by SHA-256 and keeps the
original's copyright and license records (name IDs 0, 13 and 14) in the subset.
They match the upstream OFL.txt files.

23. Roboto 3.015 (https://github.com/googlefonts/roboto-classic)
    Copyright 2011 The Roboto Project Authors
    License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1); text in `LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt`
    Files: `roboto-{300,400,700}-{normal,italic}.woff2`
    Source: release asset `Roboto_v3.015.zip`, `web/static/` (tag v3.015)
    Used for: General documentation body text

24. Roboto Mono 3.001 (https://github.com/googlefonts/robotomono)
    Copyright 2015 The Roboto Mono Project Authors
    License: SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1); text in `LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt`
    Files: `roboto-mono-{400,700}-{normal,italic}.woff2`
    Source: `fonts/ttf/` at tag v3.001 (commit 111eb14e)
    Used for: Monospaced documentation text

